+% Generated by roxygen2: do not edit by hand
+% Please edit documentation in R/net.fn.accessor.R
+\name{get_attr}
+\alias{get_attr}
+\alias{get_attr_list}
+\alias{set_attr}
+\alias{add_attr}
+\alias{append_attr}
+\alias{append_core_attr}
+\alias{remove_node_attr}
+\alias{get_core_attributes}
+\title{Get and Set Nodal Attributes in Network Models}
+\usage{
+get_attr(dat, item, posit_ids = NULL, override.null.error = FALSE)
+
+get_attr_list(dat, item = NULL)
+
+set_attr(dat, item, value, posit_ids = NULL, override.length.check = FALSE)
+
+add_attr(dat, item)
+
+append_attr(dat, item, value, n.new)
+
+append_core_attr(dat, at, n.new)
+
+remove_node_attr(dat, posit_ids)
+
+get_core_attributes()
+}
+\arguments{
+\item{dat}{Main \code{netsim_dat} object containing a \code{networkDynamic}
+object and other initialization information passed from
+\code{\link[=netsim]{netsim()}}.}
+
+\item{item}{Name of the nodal attribute. For \code{get_attr_list()}, a
+character vector of names, or \code{NULL} (default) for all attributes.}
+
+\item{posit_ids}{Positional identifiers of the nodes. For \code{get_attr()} and
+\code{set_attr()}, the nodes to get or edit, with \code{NULL} (default) for all
+nodes; for \code{remove_node_attr()}, the nodes to remove.}
+
+\item{override.null.error}{If \code{TRUE}, return \code{NULL} instead of an error
+when \code{item} does not exist (default = \code{FALSE}).}
+
+\item{value}{New values of the attribute. For \code{set_attr()}, one value per
+node, or with \code{posit_ids}, one value per selected node or a single
+value for all of them. For \code{append_attr()}, one value per new node
+or a single value for all of them.}
+
+\item{override.length.check}{If \code{TRUE}, \code{set_attr()} accepts a \code{value}
+whose length differs from the number of nodes (default = \code{FALSE}).
+Every attribute must again hold one value per node by the end of
+the time step.}
+
+\item{n.new}{Number of new nodes: for \code{append_core_attr()}, the nodes to
+add; for \code{append_attr()}, the number of values to append at the end
+of \code{item}.}
+
+\item{at}{Current time step, recorded as the entry time (\code{entrTime}) of
+the new nodes.}
+}
+\value{
+For \code{get_attr()}, the attribute vector, or its values for the
+nodes in \code{posit_ids}; for \code{get_attr_list()}, a named list of
+attribute vectors; for \code{get_core_attributes()}, a named list with a
+value of the correct type for each core attribute. The other
+functions return the updated \code{netsim_dat} object.
+}
+\description{
+Retrieve, create, and edit the nodal attributes of the main
+\code{netsim_dat} object of network models, from inside module
+functions. Each nodal attribute is a vector with one value per
+node, indexed by the positional identifiers of the nodes
+(\code{posit_ids}).
+\itemize{
+\item \code{get_attr()} returns one attribute, for all nodes or for the nodes in
+\code{posit_ids}. \code{get_attr_list()} returns several attributes as a named
+list.
+\item \code{set_attr()} replaces the values of an attribute, for all nodes or for
+the nodes in \code{posit_ids}, and creates the attribute if it does not
+exist. \code{add_attr()} creates an attribute set to \code{NA} for all nodes.
+\item \code{append_core_attr()} adds \code{n.new} nodes and sets their core
+attributes. \code{append_attr()} then adds the values of each other
+attribute for the same nodes.
+\item \code{remove_node_attr()} removes the nodes in \code{posit_ids} from every
+attribute.
+\item \code{get_core_attributes()} lists the core attributes with their types.
+}
+
+See \link{net-accessor} for an overview of the accessors.
+}
+\section{Core Attributes}{
+
+The \code{append_core_attr} function initializes the attributes necessary for
+EpiModel to work (the four core attributes are: "active", "unique_id",
+"entrTime", and "exitTime"). These attributes are used in the initialization
+phase of the simulation, to create the nodes (see
+\code{\link[=initialize.net]{initialize.net()}}); and also used when adding nodes during the
+simulation (see \code{\link[=arrivals.net]{arrivals.net()}}).
+}
+
+\section{One Value Per Node}{
+
+Every nodal attribute holds exactly one value per node, and \code{\link[=netsim]{netsim()}}
+checks this at the end of each time step. When \code{set_attr} and \code{append_attr}
+create an attribute, the nodes they do not write to are filled with \code{NA} to
+preserve that: \code{set_attr} with \code{posit_ids} fills the unselected nodes, and
+\code{append_attr} fills the nodes that predate the ones being appended. This
+means \code{append_core_attr} must be called before \code{append_attr} when adding new
+nodes, as it is what makes those nodes known to the rest of the object.
+}
+
+\section{Intended Usage}{
+
+These accessors operate on the live \code{netsim_dat} object that EpiModel
+constructs internally when a simulation starts and passes through each
+module at every time step. The expected calling context is \strong{inside a
+user-supplied module function} (e.g., a custom \code{infection.FUN},
+\code{recovery.FUN}, or arrivals/departures module) registered with
+\code{\link[=control.net]{control.net()}}.
+
+They are \emph{not} a general-purpose tool for editing the user-facing input
+or output objects of \code{\link[=netsim]{netsim()}}:
+\itemize{
+\item Calling them on a \code{\link[=param.net]{param.net()}}, \code{\link[=init.net]{init.net()}}, or \code{\link[=control.net]{control.net()}}
+object before a run will appear to succeed (those objects are also
+list-like) but produces an object that is not a valid simulation
+input.
+\item Calling them on the object returned by \code{\link[=netsim]{netsim()}} modifies only the
+saved input slot, not anything that would change the result of a
+re-run. Note also that \code{\link[=netsim]{netsim()}} strips the \verb{*.FUN} entries from
+its returned \code{control} slot, so feeding that slot back into a new
+simulation will fail.
+}
+
+For modifications outside a running simulation, use the following
+instead:
+\itemize{
+\item \strong{Editing parameters before a run:} \code{\link[=update_params]{update_params()}} for a
+\code{param.net} object, or direct list assignment
+(e.g., \code{p$inf.prob <- 0.5}).
+\item \strong{Editing init or control before a run:} direct list assignment
+(e.g., \code{ctrl$nsteps <- 1000}), or rebuild with a fresh call to the
+\code{\link[=init.net]{init.net()}} / \code{\link[=control.net]{control.net()}} constructor.
+\item \strong{Scheduled mid-simulation changes:} the \code{.param.updater.list}
+argument to \code{\link[=param.net]{param.net()}} and the \code{.control.updater.list} argument
+to \code{\link[=control.net]{control.net()}}. See the "model-parameters" vignette for the
+underlying updater module and the scenario API built on top of it.
+}
+}
+
+\section{Mutability}{
+
+The \code{set_}, \code{append_}, and \code{add_} functions DO NOT modify the
+\code{netsim_dat} object in place. The result must be assigned back to
+\code{dat} in order to be registered: \verb{dat <- set_*(dat, item, value)}.
+}
+
+\examples{
+dat <- create_dat_object(control = list(nsteps = 150))
+dat <- append_core_attr(dat, at = 1, n.new = 10)
+
+dat <- add_attr(dat, "age")
+dat <- set_attr(dat, "age", runif(10, 15, 65))
+dat <- set_attr(dat, "status", rep(c("s", "i"), c(8, 2)))
+get_attr_list(dat)
+get_attr_list(dat, c("age", "active"))
+get_attr(dat, "status")
+get_attr(dat, "status", posit_ids = c(1, 9))
+
+# Edit selected nodes
+dat <- set_attr(dat, "status", "i", posit_ids = 3)
+get_attr(dat, "status")
+
+# Add 5 nodes: core attributes first, then the others
+dat <- append_core_attr(dat, at = 2, n.new = 5)
+dat <- append_attr(dat, "status", "s", 5)
+dat <- append_attr(dat, "age", 15, 5)
+get_attr(dat, "age")
+get_attr(dat, "entrTime")
+
+}
+\seealso{
+\link{net-accessor} for an overview of the accessors, and \code{\link[=get_epi]{get_epi()}}
+and \code{\link[=get_param]{get_param()}} for the other groups; \code{\link[=arrive_nodes]{arrive_nodes()}} and
+\code{\link[=depart_nodes]{depart_nodes()}} for adding and removing nodes from the networks;
+\code{\link[=get_unique_ids]{get_unique_ids()}} and \code{\link[=get_posit_ids]{get_posit_ids()}} for converting node identifiers.
+}
